{"name":"Golden Appeal","hex":"#e6be59","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"appeal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An application to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferior court or judge to be reviewed and overturned.\nThe legal document or form by which such an application is made; also, the court case in which the application is argued.\nA person's legal right to apply to court for such a review.","An application to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferior court or judge to be reviewed and overturned."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Often followed by against (the inferior court's decision) or to (the superior court): to apply to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferior court or judge to be reviewed and overturned.","Often followed by against (the inferior court's decision) or to (the superior court): to apply to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferior court or judge to be reviewed and overturned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Appeal","blocks":[{"text":"In law, an appeal is the process in which cases or decisions are reviewed by a higher authority, where parties request a formal change to an official decision. Appeals function both as a process for error correction as well as a process of clarifying and interpreting law. Although appellate courts have existed for thousands of years, common law countries did not incorporate an affirmative right to appeal into their jurisprudence until the 19th century."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Appeal","wikidata":"Q329777"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/New_York_Court_of_Appeals_hearing_oral_arguments.jpg/500px-New_York_Court_of_Appeals_hearing_oral_arguments.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/New_York_Court_of_Appeals_hearing_oral_arguments.jpg/1280px-New_York_Court_of_Appeals_hearing_oral_arguments.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/New_York_Court_of_Appeals_hearing_oral_arguments.jpg/500px-New_York_Court_of_Appeals_hearing_oral_arguments.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The New York Court of Appeals hears oral arguments in a 2009 case involving the Atlantic Yards development in Brooklyn.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_York_Court_of_Appeals_hearing_oral_arguments.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Supreme_Court_of_Victoria_%285064240836%29.jpg/500px-Supreme_Court_of_Victoria_%285064240836%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Supreme_Court_of_Victoria_%285064240836%29.jpg/1280px-Supreme_Court_of_Victoria_%285064240836%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Supreme_Court_o